 :mcp
 [{:name "doc_bates_multi",
   :title "Add Bates numbering across files",
   :description
   "Apply one consecutive Bates sequence to an ordered list of PDFs. Each file entry has input and output paths and an optional open or permissions password. The operation first validates every input/output and computes inclusive numeric intervals; dry_run returns that allocation without writing. Existing output files are never replaced. On application, files that cannot be edited or saved are reported individually and later files continue.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_batch",
   :title "Process files and folders",
   :description
   "Run convert, ocr and/or optimize over files and folders, one file at a time. recursive defaults to false. Preserve paths relative to each selected folder inside out_dir; duplicate inputs run once. Skip unsupported files, links and the output subtree. Existing outputs receive numbered names and are never replaced. Continue after per-file errors unless stop_on_error is true. Return completed/failed/skipped counts and per-file results. Discovery is bounded to 10000 entries and 64 folder levels. Convert must be first; each step can appear once. OCR uses installed models. Optimize uses Reduce File Size settings, optionally overriding target ppi (threshold 1.5 times ppi; black-and-white images go to the larger of ppi and 300) and JPEG quality; a larger candidate keeps the original bytes. Sources and open documents are unchanged.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_fix_hairlines",
   :title "Fix hairlines",
   :description
   "Print production: strokes narrower than narrower_than points on the page (after every transformation; zero-width lines always) are given width points, in page content and form XObjects; Type 3 glyphs and tiling patterns only when asked, changed in place wherever they are used. Both widths at most 10. Returns fixed (strokes), pages, and elsewhere (glyphs and patterns changed that something outside pages also uses); nothing to fix gives 0 and no edit.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "prepress.hairlines"}
  {:name "attachment_add",
   :title "Attach a file",
   :description
   "Attach the file at path to the document (document level, the Attachments panel; not a paper-clip comment on a page). name defaults to the file's name; the attachment's key, unique in the document, is returned. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.attach"}
  {:name "attachment_delete",
   :title "Delete an attachment",
   :description
   "Remove the document-level attachment with this name (as doc_info lists it). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_convert_colours",
   :title "Convert colours",
   :description
   "Print production: every colour operator in the pages' content and the artwork it draws rewritten in the target space (to: gray, rgb or cmyk) by the standard device formulas (device spaces, ICC by component count, Lab, Indexed, Separation and DeviceN tints; patterns, shadings and inline images stay). Not a prepress separation: no ICC profile and no output intent is used. Spot colours are converted, not kept: exact through a Type 2 tint, otherwise a gray of their darkness; /None stays. preserve_black (default true) keeps pure black as 100% K / gray 0; images (default true) re-encodes 8-bit gray and RGB pictures (JPEG stays JPEG, compressed again at quality 80; CMYK written lossless; soft masks kept), and leaves indexed, CMYK, masked and other pictures as they are; annotations also converts the pages' comment and field appearances. Returns how many colours and pictures changed on how many pages, images_left (pictures not in the target that stayed), and loses_conformance (the PDF/A level and output intents the file declared: it may no longer meet them, and still declares them; standards_remove_id takes that off). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "prepress.convert_colors"}
  {:name "attachment_edit",
   :title "Edit an attachment description",
   :description
   "Change the description of a document attachment by its exact key from doc_info, or by a unique displayed name. An empty description clears it. The file and other attachment data are preserved. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_open",
   :title "Open a PDF",
   :description
   "Open a PDF file and return its document id, page count and whether it can be edited. A path that ends in open parameters, as help systems pass them (`manual.pdf#page=12`, `#nameddest=Intro` or `#Intro`), opens the file and reports its destination as link_open does; a path that names a file opens as it is.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "file.open"}
  {:name "doc_list",
   :title "List open documents",
   :description
   "List the open documents with their ids, page counts and unsaved state.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_info",
   :title "Inspect a document",
   :description
   "Metadata, page sizes and labels, bookmarks, annotations, form fields, links, layers and the Layers panel's tree (layer_order), page transitions and display times, the destination it opens at, attachments (and, for a PDF portfolio, the one it presents first), fonts, security, repair notes and the objects that could not be read.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "file.properties"}
  {:name "doc_close",
   :title "Close a document",
   :description
   "Close a document. Fails if it has unsaved changes unless discard_changes is true.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "file.close"}
  {:name "doc_set_info",
   :title "Set document metadata",
   :description
   "Set a document information entry such as Title, Author, Subject or Keywords, or a custom property under any other name (no spaces, delimiters, / or #; at most 127 bytes; doc_info lists them under custom); an empty value removes it. When the file has XMP metadata, the matching XMP property (dc:title, dc:creator, dc:description, pdf:Keywords, xmp:CreatorTool, pdf:Producer) is changed too, so viewers that read XMP first show the new value, and a custom property is kept there as pdfx:<name> when its name can be an XML name (in a PDF/A file only one already there is changed). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "page_render",
   :title "Render a page",
   :description
   "Render one page to a PNG image (default 96 dpi, at most 600). When the picture is incomplete or approximate (content cut at the page's safety budget, a picture left out because its JBIG2 mask is past a decoder limit, a colour painted in a fallback colour), a JSON part follows the image: { page, warnings: [sentence, ...] }.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "model_render",
   :title "Render a 3D model",
   :description
   "Draw a page's 3D model (a 3D annotation's PRC stream) to a PNG, framed to fill the image, with headlight shading on a white background. model is its 1-based position among the page's 3D models (default 1). direction is the view direction [x, y, z] from the eye towards the model (default [-1, 1, -1]); Z is up unless the view looks along Z. orbit, in place of direction, frames the model as a viewer's orbit control does (the same size from every side) and applies, in order: view (iso, front, right, top or back; default iso) about up (+x, +y, +z, -x, -y or -z; default +z) with the Front view looking along front (an axis perpendicular to up; default +y, or -z when y is up), then turn [yaw, pitch] in degrees (pitch looks down and stops just short of the up axis), then zoom (a factor, the result held within 0.05 to 50) about the picture point zoom_at [right, up] in picture heights from the centre (default the centre), then pan [right, up] in model radii (it moves the target, so the model moves the other way). perspective defaults to true. U3D models can't be drawn yet and give an error. Does not modify the document.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "object_list",
   :title "List editable objects",
   :description
   "List existing paragraphs, Image/Form artwork and added content once, with source kind/index references, displayed rectangles and document generation. Indexes change when content changes; use generation in object_move to reject stale references.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "object_move",
   :title "Move objects together",
   :description
   "Atomically translate 1–1000 mixed references from object_list (or with all: true every object on the page) by [dx, dy] in displayed points (right/down). Preserves glyph codes, fonts, image data and relative spacing; success is one undo step. Text used as a clipping path and vertical text are refused. A bad/stale reference refuses the entire move.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "object_copy",
   :title "Copy or cut objects together",
   :description
   "Edit ▸ Copy (cut: Cut) of 1–1000 mixed references from object_list, or with all: true every object on the page, as ⌘A then ⌘C select and copy them in Edit a PDF. The copy keeps their content operators and every resource they use (fonts, images, ExtGStates, colour spaces, patterns, shadings) and is kept for object_paste into any open document, also after this one changes or closes. cut then deletes them as one undo step. Refused when the document doesn't allow copying (cut: or changes), or when text used as a clipping path is drawn before them. Returns the count copied and their text.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "object_paste",
   :title "Paste copied objects",
   :description
   "Edit ▸ Paste of what object_copy copied, onto page of doc as page content that draws the same: where it was, or on the page it came from 18 points down and to the right, and 18 more for each further paste onto the same page; centred when that would leave it off the page. Resources join the page's under names that don't clash; into another document the fonts, images and other objects they use are copied (each once, sharing what is there; refused past 20,000 objects or 256 MB). Pasted content is untagged and in no layer. One undo step.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "text_word_count",
   :title "Word count",
   :description
   "Count Unicode words and characters on selected pages (default all), with totals and per-page counts. Table/code exclusions use PDF structure tags, not visual guesses; unclassified text is retained. Image exclusion removes Figure-tagged and invisible/OCR text. Does not run OCR. Copy permission is required. Fails rather than returning a partial total when a page cannot be read.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "file.word_count"}
  {:name "text_extract",
   :title "Extract text",
   :description
   "Extract the text of some or all pages, in reading order. With rect, only the text inside that rectangle on each page, as Column select takes it: one row per visual line, side-by-side pieces (table cells) separated by a tab. With format \"html\", each page also carries html, the same text as Copy with formatting puts on the clipboard (paragraphs, bold, italic, size, colour and font family), and styles_incomplete when some styles had to be left out. With rect, the html is that text in line order, not split into the column's rows and cells. A page whose content was cut at the renderer's limits carries truncated: true; its text is incomplete. The HTML of one call is capped at 32 MiB in total; pages past the cap carry empty html with styles_incomplete. html_truncated is set when that cap is reached or when a page's own copy was cut at its span or size cap.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.column_select"}
  {:name "text_find",
   :title "Find text",
   :description
   "Find a phrase (case-insensitive, whitespace-normalised) and return matches in page order with page and line rectangles in points (origin top-left). Reads growing batches, looking one match past the limit for a continuation. Failed pages do not discard readable matches: warnings contains up to 100 {page, error, error_truncated} entries (errors capped at 1024 UTF-8 bytes), warning_count counts failed pages, and warnings_truncated reports a capped list. complete is false after a page failure or when more matches exist; next is present only for a match-limit continuation. With stop_at_limit the search ends at the limit-th match instead of looking for one more, so a lone early match doesn't read the rest of the document.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.find"}
  {:name "text_replace",
   :title "Replace text",
   :description
   "Find and replace (Edit text ▸ Replace): each match of find, with the find bar's rules (whitespace-normalised; case-insensitive unless case_sensitive; whole_words: no letter or digit may adjoin a match), is rewritten inside its own paragraph, which keeps its fonts, sizes and colours and rewraps; the replacement takes the style of the run it lands in. A longer replacement is measured in the paragraph's fonts and is not shrunk or hyphenated: one row grows right to the page's margin, then wraps; several rows keep their width. New rows go below and nothing else moves, so they can overlap what follows, unreported; a word wider than the width overruns it. replace may be empty (deletes the match). all (default true) replaces every match on pages (default all) as one undo step; false only the first match the find bar shows (page text order; when no paragraph holds it nothing is replaced and it is reported as not_editable). Matches are left alone and counted in skipped_by when they span two paragraphs (spans_paragraphs), are invisible text over a scan (scanned_text), would need another font because the paragraph's own can't draw the new text (missing_glyphs), the paragraph can't be rewritten (refused, with refusals), or the page text holds them outside any editable paragraph, such as form fields, comments or text inside a form XObject (not_editable, counted when all). A page whose text can't be read is counted once as refused and named in refusals. Returns replaced, skipped, skipped_by, the 1-based pages changed and whether the document changed.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.replace"}
  {:name "page_rotate",
   :title "Rotate pages",
   :description
   "Rotate pages by a multiple of 90 degrees (positive is clockwise): the listed pages (default all), filtered like Acrobat's Rotate Pages by subset (all, even, odd page numbers) and orientation (all, landscape, portrait). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.rotate"}
  {:name "page_enhance_camera",
   :title "Enhance camera image",
   :description
   "Straighten a photographed document (Scan & OCR ▸ Enhance ▸ Camera image): the part of the page inside the four corners (x1, y1, … x4, y4 in top-left-origin points, any order, a convex quadrilateral; when omitted, the document's edges are found automatically, or an error says they could not be) is warped to an upright rectangle that replaces what the page shows, at the page picture's own resolution (at most 600 dpi). mode is how it looks: original, colour (default), greyscale or bw (black and white, stored losslessly). level (0–100, default 0) then cleans the photo up: even lighting so the paper turns white (casts, shadows, dark edges), more contrast, and from 60 no isolated specks; colour ink stays colour. For bw the level is the threshold (higher keeps fainter strokes black). The page's comments, links and bookmarks stay. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.enhance_camera"}
  {:name "page_enhance_scan",
   :title "Enhance scanned file",
   :description
   "Clean up scanned pages in place (Scan & OCR ▸ Enhance ▸ Scanned document). A page is a scan when its pictures cover at least half of it; the pictures covering at least a tenth of it are cleaned and written back into the same image objects at the same size and colour space (a JPEG stays a JPEG at quality 90, other grey/RGB images are stored losslessly, a 1-bit image stays 1-bit), so the page's invisible OCR text, comments, links and other content stay as they were, and an image drawn on several pages is cleaned once. level (0–100, default 50) is background removal: the paper's illumination is evened out so a grey, yellowed or unevenly lit background turns white, then the contrast is raised so faint strokes darken; colour ink stays colour. edge_shadows (default: on unless level is 0) lightens shadows along the scan's edges (book gutters, a copier's dark border). despeckle (default: from level 60) turns isolated dark specks white; it is the only change a 1-bit scan takes. Returns pages_cleaned (1-based), images (rewritten), not_scanned (pages that are no scan) and skipped ([{pages, name, reason}]: CMYK, indexed, JPEG 2000, JBIG2 or CCITT images, a scan drawn inside grouped Form artwork, broken data, or nothing to change). One undoable step; none when nothing changed.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.enhance"}
  {:name "page_delete",
   :title "Delete pages",
   :description "Delete pages. Undoable until saved.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.delete"}
  {:name "page_move",
   :title "Move pages",
   :description
   "Move pages so the first of them lands at position `to` (1-based, counted before the move). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "page_reverse",
   :title "Reverse pages",
   :description
   "Reverse the order of pages among the positions they occupy: the listed pages (at least two), or the whole document when pages is omitted. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.reverse"}
  {:name "page_insert_blank",
   :title "Insert a blank page",
   :description
   "Insert a blank page so it becomes page `at`. Size defaults to the neighbouring page. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.insert_blank"}
  {:name "page_insert_file",
   :title "Insert pages from a file",
   :description
   "Insert pages of another PDF so the first becomes page `at`. Its bookmarks come along, collapsed under one bookmark named after the file, placed among the document's bookmarks where the pages went. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.insert"}
  {:name "page_extract",
   :title "Extract pages",
   :description
   "Copy pages into a new PDF (links, bookmarks, fields and layers that belong to them come along). separate: true writes each page as its own file into out_dir; delete: true removes the pages from this document afterwards (undoable).",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.extract"}
  {:name "doc_combine",
   :title "Combine files",
   :description
   "Combine files, in order, into one PDF (bookmarks are kept under one entry per file). Images (PNG, JPEG, TIFF, GIF, BMP, JPEG 2000), .txt files and Office documents (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OpenDocument, RTF; through an installed LibreOffice) are made into PDFs first. pages optionally chooses each file's pages, in step with paths: a range such as \"1-3, 6\" or null for all pages. passwords, also in step with paths, opens encrypted files (the open password, or the permissions password where a file's security doesn't allow copying pages; null for none). The result is not encrypted. Passwords are never echoed back. groups, also in step with paths, splits a file around others: entries with the same number (they must name the same path) are one file, copied once, so it keeps one bookmark at its first page, its links and its form fields; null for a file of its own. A group uses its first entry's password. When two files' forms name the same field, field_conflicts says what happens: \"rename\" (the default) keeps the fields separate by renaming the later one (Text1 becomes Text1-1) and the result lists renamed_fields as [[old, new], …] — scripts that refer to the old name are not rewritten; \"merge\" makes them one field, as before.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.combine"}
  {:name "doc_create_multiple",
   :title "Create PDF from multiple files",
   :description
   "Convert several files (PDFs, PNG/JPEG/JPEG 2000/TIFF/GIF/BMP images, .txt files, Office documents through an installed LibreOffice) to PDF in one run. mode \"combine\" (default) joins them, in order, into one PDF with a bookmark per file; pages optionally chooses each file's pages, in step with paths (a range such as \"1-3, 6\" or null). mode \"separate\" writes one PDF per file into out_dir (files that are already PDFs are skipped; existing files are never overwritten) and reports each file's result.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "create.multiple"}
  {:name "doc_split",
   :title "Split a document",
   :description
   "Split into several files written to out_dir: every N pages, before given pages, at top-level bookmarks (bookmarks: true; files named after them, repeated titles get -2, -3), or by file size (max_mb). Files are <name>-partK.pdf.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.split"}
  {:name "bookmark_rename",
   :title "Rename a bookmark",
   :description "Change a bookmark's title. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "bookmark_delete",
   :title "Delete a bookmark",
   :description
   "Delete a bookmark and the bookmarks under it. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "bookmark_move",
   :title "Move a bookmark",
   :description
   "Move a bookmark (with its children) under another parent, or within its level. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "bookmark_set_page",
   :title "Set a bookmark's page",
   :description "Point a bookmark at another page. Undoable.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "page_number",
   :title "Number pages",
   :description
   "Label a range of pages (e.g. i, ii, iii for front matter, or A-1, A-2 for an appendix). Later pages keep their labels. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_fields",
   :title "List form fields",
   :description
   "Every interactive form field: name, type (text, checkbox, radio, combo, list, button, signature), value, options, page, rect (top-left-origin points) and rotation (0, 90, 180 or 270 degrees counterclockwise), read-only and required flags. A calculated field includes calculate: {op, fields} or {notation} as form_set_props takes them, or {script} for a custom Calculate script (set with form_set_script). Push buttons include caption (first widget's normal label) and captions [{widget, caption}] for all widgets (1-based). Radio groups include on_widgets, the 1-based numbers of the buttons that are on (buttons sharing an option tell apart only there). A check box whose widgets have different on states also lists them as options, and which one is checked (null when none). Combo and list boxes include selected: the 1-based positions in options of the selected ones, which tells apart options that share an export value.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_reset",
   :title "Clear form",
   :description
   "Reset fields to their default values: all of them, or only those listed. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.add.text_table"}
  {:name "stamp_custom",
   :title "Add a custom stamp",
   :description
   "Stamp a picture: a PDF page (file_page, default 1, kept as vector content in a form XObject) or an image file. Either centred at at [x, y] (points from the top-left of the displayed page) at its natural size, at most 200 pt, or fitted inside rect [x0, y0, x1, y1] (the same coordinates; each side 1–14400 pt), scaled to keep its shape and centred in the box. Like at, rect is not clipped to the page. Pass at or rect, not both. name labels it (default: the file name). line adds a text line under the picture with {name} (the author), {date} and {time} filled in now, as a dynamic stamp. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "comment.stamp"}
  {:name "model_add",
   :title "Add a 3D model",
   :description
   "Add a 3D model (Acrobat: Rich Media ▸ Add 3D): the U3D or PRC file at path, recognised by its first bytes, as a 3D annotation in rect [x0, y0, x1, y1] (points from the top-left of the displayed page; each side 1–14400 pt; at most 256 MiB). Its poster, what prints and what readers show until the model is activated, is the picture at poster (a PDF page, poster_page default 1, or an image) fitted inside rect keeping its shape and centred; without poster, a frame labelled \"3D model\". activation: click (default), page_open or page_visible. name is its description (default: the file name). No views are added: readers open the model on its own default view. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_set_image",
   :title "Set an image field's picture",
   :description
   "Show an image file (PNG, JPEG, TIFF, GIF or BMP) in an image field or button, scaled to fit and centred (what clicking an image field does). On an XFA form the picture is kept in its data too (base64, as Designer saves it) and the form shows it from there. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_tab_order",
   :title "Set the tab order",
   :description
   "Set the tab order of pages (default all): row (top to bottom, left to right; right to left in a document bound on the right), column, structure, or annotations (unspecified). Or order tabs manually: `field` with `move` earlier|later moves that field one place on its page. Without `order` or `field` it only reads. Returns the resulting order of fields (`tab_order`) and each page's tab order (`page_tabs`, as Page properties ▸ Tab Order shows it). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_calculation_order",
   :title "Read or set the calculation order",
   :description
   "The calculated fields in the order they calculate (Acrobat: Set Field Calculation Order), each with its `formula` (as form_fields shows calculate), the fields it reads (`reads`; a script's names built at run time aren't known) and its `issues`: missing_field (it reads `field`, which the form doesn't have, so it gets no value there), runs_too_early (it reads `field`, which calculates after it, so it shows a stale value), cycle (it reads `fields`, which read it back: no order fixes that, a formula has to change) and not_in_order (the PDF's order leaves it out, so other viewers may not calculate it) and built_names (its script also reads fields by names it builds at run time, which aren't checked). `extra` lists entries of the PDF's order that calculate nothing. Without a change it only reads. Changes, one at a time: `order` (these fields first, in this order, then the other calculated fields in their order), `field` with `move` earlier|later (one place), or `fix` true (only what must move moves, so every field calculates after the fields it reads, and the extra entries go). A change recalculates the form. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.calculation_order"}
  {:name "doc_export_data",
   :title "Export comments or form data",
   :description
   "Write comments and/or form data to path; the extension picks the format: .xfdf or .fdf (comments and/or fields), .xml, .csv or .txt (form data). For an XFA form, .xml is its data alone (rooted at the form's root data node, as Acrobat exports it) and .xdp an XML Data Package holding the whole datasets. what: all (default), comments, fields.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_import_data",
   :title "Import comments or form data",
   :description
   "Import comments and/or field values from an XFDF, FDF, XML, CSV or tab-delimited text file (detected from its content), or the comments of another PDF, each onto the page with the same number (comments on pages past this document's last page are left out). Comments with the same name are replaced; values go through the form's formats and validation. For an XFA form, an XDP, datasets or data XML file replaces the form's data: a laid-out form is laid out again from it (rows included) and its calculations run. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_delete_field",
   :title "Delete a field",
   :description
   "Delete a form field and all its widgets, or with widget only that one: one radio button of a group (widget n is the nth of the radio group's options in form_fields), or one copy of a duplicated field. A field's last widget takes the field with it. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "redact_clear",
   :title "Remove redaction marks",
   :description
   "Remove every redaction mark without applying it. Undoable.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "printers",
   :title "List printers",
   :description
   "The printers the system's print spooler knows (CUPS on macOS and Linux), with the default marked.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "print_color_profiles",
   :title "List printer colour profiles",
   :description
   "The RGB and grey ICC profiles installed on this computer that doc_print can convert the pages into (color_management app): name, path and color_space. Windows: the system colour folder; macOS: the ColorSync folders; Linux: the shared and per-user icc folders. CMYK profiles are left out: the printed pictures are RGB.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "printer_options",
   :title "List printer options",
   :description
   "A printer driver's own job options (CUPS: from its PPD), such as the paper tray, paper type or finishing: key, label, group, default and choices. Pass chosen values to doc_print as options. Empty on Windows, where the driver's preferences window holds them.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "content_list",
   :title "List added content",
   :description
   "Text and images added with page_add_text/page_add_image (or Edit a PDF ▸ Add content), per page with a 1-based index, rect (points from the top-left of the page), and text style; text painted in gray or CMYK also has gray (its level) or cmyk ([c, m, y, k]).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.text"}
  {:name "content_update",
   :title "Edit added content",
   :description
   "Move/resize (rect), retype (text) or restyle (font, size, bold, italic, color or gray or cmyk as page_add_text takes them, align, char_spacing in points) an added item (page, index from content_list). Images: rotate (degrees, multiple of 90, counter-clockwise), flip_h / flip_v (toggle), crop [left, bottom, right, top] as fractions trimmed, image (a file that replaces the picture). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "content_delete",
   :title "Delete added content",
   :description
   "Delete an added item (page, index from content_list). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "link_list",
   :title "List links",
   :description
   "Every link: page, 1-based index (for link_edit/link_delete), rect (points from the top-left of the page), and where it goes (url, or to_page with its zoom). A relative url also has resolved_url, the address resolved against the document's base URI (catalog /URI /Base); a link active only in its /QuadPoints has active_areas, one rect per quadrilateral. With text_links: true, also the web and email addresses written as plain page text with no link over them, which the viewer opens on a click: page, rects (one per line), url, and blocked (why it won't open) when the link check refuses it. Only http, https and mailto addresses are found. At most 100 pages are read per call, from text_links_from (default 1); text_links_next_page then gives the page to continue from.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "link_open",
   :title "Open a linked PDF",
   :description
   "Follow a local GoToR link in PdfCraft: open the referenced PDF as a new document, respecting --root. page and index use link_list numbering. A named destination is looked up in the target, as the app does; one the target doesn't define is reported with a warning. Absolute file specifications require allow_absolute: true after reviewing the target; relative links need no opt-in.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "link_add",
   :title "Add a link",
   :description
   "Add a link over rect on page that opens url or goes to to_page, shown at zoom: fit_page (default), fit_width, fit_height, fit_visible, actual, inherit (keep the reader's zoom) or a percentage. Appearance: visible (rectangle), color, width 1-3, highlight none/invert/outline/inset. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.link"}
  {:name "link_edit",
   :title "Edit a link",
   :description
   "Change a link's rect, destination (url, or to_page and zoom as in link_add; a new to_page keeps the link's zoom, a zoom alone keeps its page) or appearance. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "link_run_javascript",
   :title "Run a link's JavaScript",
   :description
   "Run the JavaScript action of link `index` on page `page` (1-based, from link_list: index is the link's place among the page's annotations), as clicking it does: event.type Link, event.name Mouse Up, event.target the document, this.pageNum the link's page, in the document's script realm. answers reply to its popup menus, response dialogs and alerts in order (null cancels a menu or response; missing answers do too); a menu with no items answers null without using one. Field changes and resetForm are one undoable step; a script that fails commits nothing and its requests are dropped. Returns alerts, console, requests (page, url, open_doc and others, never carried out), error and result.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "link_delete",
   :title "Delete a link",
   :description
   "Delete one link (page, index from link_list). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "links_from_urls",
   :title "Create links from URLs",
   :description
   "Find web addresses (http://, https://, www.) in the text of every page and make them clickable links, leaving out text on a layer the viewer hides (layer_set). Returns the URLs. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.links_from_urls"}
  {:name "links_remove",
   :title "Remove all links",
   :description
   "Remove every link in the document (or on the given pages). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.remove_links"}
  {:name "measure_distance",
   :title "Measure distance",
   :description
   "Add an undoable two-point distance annotation using the scale of the first point's viewport.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.distance"}
  {:name "measure_perimeter",
   :title "Measure perimeter",
   :description
   "Add an undoable connected-line length annotation. To include a closing edge, repeat the first point at the end.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.perimeter"}
  {:name "measure_area",
   :title "Measure area",
   :description
   "Add an undoable area annotation from a simple polygon. The last edge closes automatically.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.area"}
  {:name "measure_info",
   :title "Read a measurement",
   :description
   "Calculate a live distance, perimeter or area, deltas, angle and scale without adding an annotation. Incomplete paths are allowed.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.info"}
  {:name "measure_list",
   :title "List measurements",
   :description
   "Saved measurement annotations with calculated values, scale and vertices in display coordinates. Measurements with unsupported imported formats (compound or fractional units, non-rectilinear scales) or invalid geometry are listed under unsupported with a reason.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "measure_scale",
   :title "Set or read a measurement scale",
   :description
   "Read the scale at a point, or add a rectangular viewport using a ratio (page_distance in page_unit on the page = distance in unit, e.g. 1 mm = 50 mm for a 1:50 plan; page_unit defaults to unit), units_per_point or two calibration points and their real-world distance. Existing measurements retain their original scales. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.scale"}
  {:name "measure_snap",
   :title "Snap a measurement vertex",
   :description
   "Snap a point to vector paths, endpoints, midpoints or intersections. Coordinates and tolerance are in display points. Bounded extraction reports truncated geometry.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.snap"}
  {:name "measure_export",
   :title "Export measurements as CSV",
   :description
   "Atomically write saved measurement values, labels, authors and scale ratios as spreadsheet-safe CSV. Returns how many unsupported measurements were left out.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "measure.export"}
  {:name "comment_list",
   :title "List comments",
   :description
   "Every comment (annotation other than links, form widgets and pop-ups) with its page, index, id, type, author, text, date, rectangle, colour, review status, checkmark and replies (each with its own status and checkmark); the points that shape a line, polygon or callout, and a callout's text box. Annotations grouped with a comment (/RT /Group) are listed once, as that comment with its attributes, and named in its `group`. comment_delete deletes just the member named, as Acrobat does (Replace Text's strikeout and caret go together).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_reply",
   :title "Reply to a comment",
   :description "Add a reply to a comment's thread. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_set_status",
   :title "Set a comment's status",
   :description
   "Set a comment's review status (Acrobat: Set status), recorded as a status reply. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "sign_list",
   :title "List and validate signatures",
   :description
   "Every signature field with its validation: status (valid, unknown = intact but the signer isn't trusted, invalid, unsigned), signer and certificate, date, reason, location, certification level, page and rect, whether PdfCraft draws that state into the signature's own appearance as displayed (verdict_shown; never written to the file), the revision it covers and changes made after signing (none, allowed, disallowed), with Acrobat-style explanations.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "sign_id_create",
   :title "Create a digital ID",
   :description
   "Create a self-signed digital ID and save it as a password-protected .p12 file (Acrobat: Configure a new digital ID ▸ Create a new digital ID ▸ Save to file). Default key: 2048-bit RSA, valid 5 years.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "sign_windows_ids",
   :title "List Windows store digital IDs",
   :description
   "Windows: signing identities in the Current User Personal certificate store (certificate details and the windows: reference sign_document takes). Private keys remain in CNG; Windows may ask permission to use them. `unusable` lists the store's other certificates with why they can't sign (no private key, an unsupported key type, a key CNG can't open).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "sign.digital"}
  {:name "sign_keychain_ids",
   :title "List Keychain digital IDs",
   :description
   "macOS: the signing identities in the user's keychains (certificate details and the keychain: reference sign_document takes). The private keys stay in the Keychain, which may ask the user to allow their use.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "sign.digital"}
  {:name "sign_document",
   :title "Sign a document",
   :description
   "Sign with a digital ID (a .p12/.pfx path, or on macOS a Keychain identity: \"keychain:<common name or fingerprint>\" from sign_keychain_ids, or on Windows a store identity: \"windows:<common name or fingerprint>\" from sign_windows_ids) and save the signed file to `out` (signing always saves, as in Acrobat; the document then shows the signed file). Sign an existing empty signature field (`field`), or a new one on `page` at `rect` (omit rect for an invisible signature). certify: no_changes, form_fill or comments makes a certification signature. graphic shows a picture where the signer's name would be large (Acrobat: Configure Signature Appearance): {\"image\": path} (PNG or JPEG), {\"text\": name} (typed in the Fill & Sign script font) or {\"strokes\": [[[x, y], …], …]} (y up, the drawing pad 1 wide); it needs a visible signature. appearance chooses what a visible signature shows (default: name, date and labels; reason, location and distinguished_name are off unless turned on). labels gives the words of its labels, e.g. in another language (default English: \"Digitally signed by\", \"DN: \", \"Reason: \", \"Location: \", \"Date: \"; include the separator); each must be in Western European characters (Windows-1252), the only ones the signature's font draws, or the call is refused naming the label and character. PAdES B-B, SHA-256 (SHA-384 for P-384 keys). On a dynamic (XFA) form, run_form_scripts: true runs the field's own signing scripts: preSign just before signing, so what it changes is signed too (form_scripts.changed lists each field it changed, with the values before and after), and postSign after, left unsaved. Without it they don't run, and form_scripts.skipped says the field has them.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "sign.digital"}
  {:name "sign_trust",
   :title "Trust certificates",
   :description
   "Add certificates (.cer/.crt/.pem/.der, a .p7b/.p7c bundle, or the certificates in a .p12 with `password`) to the trusted certificates used to validate signatures, or clear the list (clear: true). Every open document is revalidated. Returns the trusted list.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_mark",
   :title "Mark a comment with a checkmark",
   :description
   "Mark or unmark a comment with a checkmark (Acrobat: Mark with checkmark), recorded as a private reply. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_lock",
   :title "Lock a comment",
   :description
   "Lock or unlock a comment (Properties ▸ Locked). Locked comments can't be moved, resized, restyled or deleted; their text stays editable. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "layer_set",
   :title "Show or hide a layer",
   :description
   "Show or hide a layer (optional content group), as the Layers panel's eye icon does. layer is its name as doc_info lists it (every layer with that name) or its 1-based position in that list. A view setting: page_render draws with it, and the file doesn't change. Returns every layer with its visibility.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comments_hide",
   :title "Hide all comments",
   :description
   "Hide or show every comment on the page (fields and links still draw). A view setting: the file doesn't change.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "comment.hide_all"}
  {:name "view_reading_colors",
   :title "Set reading colours",
   :description
   "Set the document's reading colours (Acrobat's Replace Document Colors, in the Reading Options): solid text and line-art paints are remapped for readability and the page clears to the background colour in page_render. A view setting: the file doesn't change. mode is one of: off, black-on-white, white-on-black, yellow-on-black, green-on-black, or custom (which takes text and background as #RRGGBB). only_black maps only near-black paints (default false) and line_art also maps line-art paints (default true); both override the mode's preset. A flag that differs from the mode's preset default makes the returned mode read custom, because the resulting params no longer match any preset. Returns the resulting setting.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.reading_options"}
  {:name "comments_summarize",
   :title "Summarize comments",
   :description
   "Make a PDF summarising every comment (number, author, type, date, text, replies), sorted by page, author, date or type.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "comment.summarize"}
  {:name "comment_edit",
   :title "Edit a comment",
   :description
   "Change a comment's text, colour, opacity (the whole comment's, or its fill's and text's own), line width, font size (text box/typewriter/callout), fill (rectangle/oval/polygon/text box/callout; \"none\" removes it), border colour (`border_color`, text box/typewriter/callout; \"text\" gives it the text's colour again), rectangle (rectangle/oval/text box/stamp, or a callout's text box: its arrow point stays and its leader line re-attaches), position (`move` [dx, dy] in points) or shape (`points`: a line's two ends, the corners of connected lines, a polygon or a cloud, or a callout's arrow point and knee, as comment_list gives them). Stamps keep their original appearance when resized. One undo step.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_image_preview",
   :title "Preview image signature layers",
   :description
   "Return a PNG of the page without the selected image signature/initials (layer=background, default), or its embedded image with alpha (layer=image). Includes the displayed rectangle, document rotation, image_rotation (how far clockwise the image is shown turned) and annotation opacity. Cache these layers for live placement/resizing; commit once with comment_edit. Does not change the document or undo history.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_delete",
   :title "Delete a comment",
   :description
   "Delete a comment with its pop-up and replies, or one reply (its id, or page and index, from comment_list) with its pop-up and the replies to it; the comment and its other replies stay. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "comment_popup",
   :title "Open, close or move a comment's pop-up",
   :description
   "Open or close a comment's pop-up window (open), or move it (rect, in page view coordinates as comment_list reports). A comment without a pop-up gets one beside it. Text boxes, Fill & Sign marks and replies have none of their own. Undoable.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "protect.password"}
  {:name "doc_unprotect",
   :title "Remove security",
   :description
   "Remove password security (the document must have been opened with its permissions password, or have none). Applied by the next doc_save. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "protect.remove"}
  {:name "page_replace",
   :title "Replace pages",
   :description
   "Replace the content of pages with pages of another PDF (same count). Links, comments, form fields and bookmarks on the original pages stay, as in Acrobat. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.replace"}
  {:name "page_duplicate",
   :title "Duplicate pages",
   :description
   "Insert copies of pages so the first copy becomes page `at`, or after the last of them when `at` is left out (fonts and images are shared, not copied). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "page.duplicate"}
  {:name "doc_watermark",
   :title "Add watermark",
   :description
   "Add a watermark to pages: text, or a picture from `file` (an image, or page `file_page` of a PDF) at `scale` of the page (default 0.5); rotated (degrees counter-clockwise, default 45), semi-transparent (opacity 0–1, default 0.5), text fitted to the page unless font_size is given (Thai drawn from PdfCraft's built-in Thai face; a build without one refuses it), on top unless behind: true; moved from the page centre by `offset_x` (right) and `offset_y` (up) points (default 0). replace: true swaps out existing ones. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.watermark"}
  {:name "doc_background",
   :title "Add background",
   :description
   "Fill page backgrounds with a colour, or a picture from `file` (an image, or page `file_page` of a PDF) fitted at `scale` (default 1), behind the content. A page that paints its own opaque white backdrop would hide it, so that backdrop is replaced unless replace_backdrop is false (removing the background turns it back on where that is still safe, and doc_remove_marks warns about the pages where it isn't); a scanned page's picture still hides it (doc_backdrops lists both). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.background"}
  {:name "doc_printer_marks",
   :title "Add printer marks",
   :description
   "Print production: trim marks, bleed marks (dashed, at the bleed box), registration targets, colour bars and a page-information line (label, page n of N, date) drawn outside the trim box as a removable page mark, in registration colour (Separation All, so on every plate) except the process-ink colour bars; the page is widened by make_room points a side when the marks would fall outside it (the trim box stays). replace (default true) replaces marks added before. Undoable; doc_remove_marks kind printer_marks takes them off.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "prepress.marks"}
  {:name "doc_backdrops",
   :title "List page backdrops",
   :description
   "Pages that paint their own backdrop, which hides a background added behind the content: `fill` (an opaque white fill doc_background can replace) or `image` (a page-sized picture, e.g. a scan, that still hides it). Pages are 1-based; pages without one are left out.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.background"}
  {:name "doc_remove_marks",
   :title
   "Remove header & footer, watermark, background or printer marks",
   :description
   "Remove every header and footer, watermark, background or printer marks PdfCraft (or a compatible tool) added. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_export_images",
   :title "Export pages as images",
   :description
   "Write pages as PNG, JPEG or TIFF files (`<name>_page_<n>.png|jpg|tif`) into a folder, at a resolution (default 150 dpi). JPEG and TIFF are flattened onto white paper. A page too large for the renderer at that resolution is drawn at the most it allows, listed in `lower_dpi` ({page, dpi}). Includes unsaved edits.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "export.image"}
  {:name "accessibility_autotag_preview",
   :title "Preview automatic tags",
   :description
   "Propose paragraph and heading tags for visible text blocks on one page. Returns page bounds, tentative roles and reasons. Does not change the PDF or claim accessibility compliance. Images, tables, lists, annotations and existing structure require separate review.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_autotag_apply",
   :title "Automatically tag text-only PDF",
   :description
   "Write marked content, a Document structure element, paragraph tags and a parent tree for every text object in an untagged, text-only PDF. Refuses graphics, images, annotations, forms, existing tags and malformed streams before changing anything. Review all resulting roles; this does not certify accessibility. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_autotag_form_fields",
   :title "Tag form fields",
   :description
   "Write `/Form` tags, widget structure-parent keys, and a parent tree for all page widgets in an untagged AcroForm. Existing tag trees are refused for review. Text, figures, links, and other content are not tagged.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.autotag_fields"}
  {:name "accessibility_check",
   :title "Check for accessibility",
   :description
   "Run the Accessibility Checker's full check (32 rules in 7 categories: document, page_content, forms, alternate_text, tables, lists, headings). Each rule is passed, failed (with findings and pages), manual (needs a person) or skipped. Findings on locatable figures, annotations and form widgets include bbox_user_space in PDF coordinates. Colour contrast is off unless all is true; rules (ids such as tagged-pdf, figures-alt-text) or categories narrow the check; pages limit the page rules.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.check"}
  {:name "accessibility_find_untagged",
   :title "Find untagged content",
   :description
   "Find untagged painted page content, annotations, and form widgets. This focused check does not modify the PDF or claim that its other accessibility rules pass.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.find_untagged"}
  {:name "accessibility_report",
   :title "Accessibility report",
   :description
   "Run the full check and write the accessibility report (HTML) to path; returns the results too. Takes the same options as accessibility_check.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.report"}
  {:name "accessibility_review_record",
   :title "Accessibility review record",
   :description
   "Compare the same accessibility rules on two open versions of a PDF and write a JSON record to path. Includes document SHA-256 hashes, before/after rule statuses and finding counts, changed rules, and rules still needing review. Does not change either PDF or claim accessibility compliance. Open the original and edited copies as separate documents.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_review_save",
   :title "Save accessibility review decisions",
   :description
   "Write a local JSON sidecar for an open PDF with rule-level human review decisions. The sidecar records the PDF SHA-256; replacing one tied to different bytes requires replace: true. Does not change the PDF or assert compliance.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_review_load",
   :title "Open accessibility review decisions",
   :description
   "Read a local review sidecar only when its recorded SHA-256 matches the open PDF. Returns the decisions without changing the PDF.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_review_html",
   :title "Accessibility review summary",
   :description
   "Compare two open versions of a PDF and write a self-contained HTML summary of the same evidence as accessibility_review_record: document hashes, outcome counts, rule changes, and rules still requiring review. Does not change either PDF or claim accessibility compliance.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_fix",
   :title "Fix an accessibility problem",
   :description
   "Apply the checker's automatic fix for a rule: primary-language (value: the language, e.g. en-US), title (value: the title; default the current title or file name; also shows it in the title bar) or tab-order (every page tabs in structure order). Returns the rule's new status. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_figures",
   :title "List figures",
   :description
   "The tagged figures (Figure elements, through the role map) in document order: figure number, page, alternate text and where the figure is drawn (top-left-origin points).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.alt_text"}
  {:name "accessibility_set_alt",
   :title "Set alternate text",
   :description
   "Set a figure's alternate text (alt; empty or omitted clears it), or mark it decorative (decorative: true: its content becomes an artifact and the figure leaves the tags). figure is a number from accessibility_figures. Returns the figures. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.alt_text"}
  {:name "accessibility_tags",
   :title "List structure tags",
   :description
   "List reachable indirect structure tags in document order with PDF object number, generation, nearest indirect parent, depth, page, type, title, actual text, alternate text, language, a table's summary and a header cell's scope, one page at a time: count is how many tags match, next the offset of the following page (null at the end). types, pages and max_depth keep only some tags. Inline tag dictionaries have no stable object reference and are not listed.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.tags"}
  {:name "accessibility_tag_content",
   :title "List tag content",
   :description
   "List the marked-content references directly owned by one reachable indirect structure tag, including page, MCID and extracted text.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "a11y.tags"}
  {:name "accessibility_set_tag_property",
   :title "Edit tag property",
   :description
   "Set or clear one property of a reachable indirect structure tag. Use object and generation from accessibility_tags. Properties: type, title, actual_text, alternate_text, language, summary (Table tags: the table's Summary attribute), scope (TH tags: Row, Column or Both). Summary and scope are written in the tag's Table attribute object (/A, /O /Table); the role map decides a tag's type. Empty or omitted value clears text properties, summary and scope; type requires a nonempty PDF name. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_mark_tag_artifact",
   :title "Mark tag content as artifact",
   :description
   "Mark a reachable leaf structure tag's direct marked content as an artifact and remove the tag from the reading structure. Use object and generation from accessibility_tags. Tags with child structure elements, no direct marked content, content not found on its page, or content that a damaged or undecodable content stream may hide or change are rejected. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_layout_table_to_blocks",
   :title "Change layout table to blocks",
   :description
   "Turn a table used only for layout (label and value pairs, a letterhead grid) into plain blocks in one step: the Table tag, its THead/TBody/TFoot and TR tags become Div, its TH, TD and Caption tags P (Div when they hold tags of their own). Content, reading order and the tags inside cells stay; a table nested in a cell stays a table; Table attributes (Summary, Scope, spans) are removed, other attributes kept. The tag's type must be Table after the role map; use object and generation from accessibility_tags. Undoable. Returns the tags as accessibility_tags does.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "accessibility_move_tag",
   :title "Move structure tag",
   :description
   "Move a reachable indirect structure tag before or after a direct sibling in their parent's /K array, changing tagged reading order without changing page appearance. Use object and generation values from accessibility_tags. Rejects distinct parents, duplicate references and positions that are already current. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "form_merge_data",
   :title "Merge data files into spreadsheet",
   :description
   "Collect the field values of form data files (FDF, XFDF) or filled-in PDF forms into one CSV file at path: a column per field name, a row per file. Returns the row and column counts.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.merge_data"}
  {:name "js_run",
   :title "Run JavaScript",
   :description
   "Run Acrobat JavaScript in the document, as the JavaScript console does (or as push button `field`'s Mouse Up script when field is given; on a laid-out XFA form, `field` runs that button's XFA click script instead, JavaScript or FormCalc, which can add and remove rows and show or hide subforms). The form object model is available: this/getField, event, app, util, console, display, color, and the document-level scripts (except the PDF container scripts when XFA layout is active; they remain available through js_document_scripts). Field changes and resetForm are applied as one undoable step; returns the script's and subsequent field scripts' alerts (each with its message, title, icon and buttons, in order; AcroForm replies consume ordered answers; missing replies cancel input or use the alert button set's safe default), console output, requests (print, page, url, submit, attachment), error, and the errors of document-level scripts that failed (the rest still ran), plus warnings from applying the changes.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "tools.js_console"}
  {:name "js_page",
   :title "Run page actions",
   :description
   "Read the document at `page`, as the viewer does when that page becomes the one being read: the actions the page it was at runs as it closes, then this page's open actions (its own, and its annotations' page-open and page-visible actions, which start an animation made with the LaTeX animate package), in the document's JavaScript context, which buttons, the console and timers share. Fields the actions show or hide change only how the document is shown, and page_render draws them so; values they change are applied as one undoable step. Returns the actions' alerts, console output, requests and errors, the pages showing a field they showed or hid, and when the next timer falls due on the script clock (js_advance moves it).",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "js_advance",
   :title "Advance the script clock",
   :description
   "Move the document's script clock on by `ms` milliseconds and run the timers its scripts set (app.setInterval, app.setTimeOut) as they fall due on the way, in order, as the viewer runs them over time: an animation shows its next frames. Fields timers show or hide change only how the document is shown, and page_render draws them so. A timer's alerts and requests go to its console output instead. Returns how many timers ran, their console output and errors, the pages showing a field they showed or hid, the clock, and when the next timer falls due.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "js_document_scripts",
   :title "Document JavaScripts",
   :description
   "List the document-level JavaScripts (name and source), which define functions field scripts use.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "tools.document_js"}
  {:name "js_set_document_script",
   :title "Edit a document JavaScript",
   :description
   "Add or replace the document-level JavaScript `name` with `script`, or delete it (script omitted). Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "tools.document_js"}
  {:name "form_set_script",
   :title "Set a field's JavaScript",
   :description
   "Field Properties ▸ Run custom script: set field's JavaScript for event keystroke, format, validate or calculate (the field's actions; calculated fields join the calculation order) or mouse_up (a button's action). Omit script to remove it. The scripts use Acrobat's object model (event.value, event.rc, getField, util.printf, …) and run when the field changes. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.prepare"}
  {:name "doc_export_office",
   :title "Export to Word, PowerPoint, HTML, RTF or Markdown",
   :description
   "Export a PDF ▸ Word (.docx), PowerPoint (.pptx, one slide per page), HTML (.html, one file with images inline), RTF (.rtf) or Markdown (.md or .markdown: pipe tables, images left out), chosen by path's extension: text, headings, bold and italic. HTML uses rich styling by default; set html_mode to simple for CSS-free headings, paragraphs, emphasis and tables. Simple HTML keeps text and inline images but omits colour and layout styling. Word uses inferred tables, bordered only along the grid lines the page draws, and positioned editable shapes on pages with artwork, rotated or large text; each source page retains its size. Font matching and vector graphics remain limited. Export reads forms 50 deep and up to 50 000 a page, counting forms the page draws itself. Pages that go past either limit, or that have pictures past what one export may hold or decode, are listed in truncated_pages, with a warning; what was left out is missing.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "export.docx"}
  {:name "pdfa_verify",
   :title "Verify PDF/A",
   :description
   "Standards ▸ Verify PDF/A compliance: the PDF/A-2b or 3b rules the document breaks (ISO 19005 clause, message, page, whether Save as PDF/A can fix it), plus what it declares.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "standards.pdfa"}
  {:name "print_readiness",
   :title "Print readiness",
   :description
   "Verification only. Reports effective image resolution where each image is drawn (not against the page size), page boxes and bleed past the trim, output intents, fonts that are not embedded, and the PDF/A-2b structural result. Does not modify the document, embed fonts, invent a press profile, or check PDF/X.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "pdfa_convert",
   :title "Save as PDF/A",
   :description
   "Standards ▸ Save as PDF/A: fix what can be fixed for PDF/A-2b or 3b (XMP identification and metadata, an sRGB output intent, forbidden actions and JavaScript, annotation print flags, image interpolation, encryption, the file header, the file identifier). Returns what was fixed and what remains (e.g. fonts that aren't embedded). Undoable; save the document to keep it.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "standards.pdfa"}
  {:name "standards_remove_id",
   :title "Remove PDF/A or PDF/X identification",
   :description
   "Remove what identifies the document as PDF/A (its pdfaid: XMP properties) or PDF/X (GTS_PDFXVersion and GTS_PDFXConformance, in the document information and as pdfxid: or pdfx: XMP properties), e.g. after edits it no longer meets. Output intents and other metadata stay. Fails when the document declares nothing of the kind. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "action_list",
   :title "List actions",
   :description
   "Action Wizard: the built-in actions (name, description, steps) and every step an action can use (id, label, whether it takes a text argument).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "actions.wizard"}
  {:name "action_run",
   :title "Run an action",
   :description
   "Action Wizard: run a built-in action (action: its name) or a list of steps ([{step, arg}], ids from action_list) on each PDF in paths, writing the results into folder under the same names. Returns each file's step log or error.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "actions.wizard"}
  {:name "doc_compare",
   :title "Compare files",
   :description
   "Compare the text of two open documents: other is the older version, doc the newer. Returns counts and each change (replaced, inserted, deleted) with the old and new text, pages (1-based) and rectangles (points, origin bottom-left).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "doc.compare"}
  {:name "doc_compare_report",
   :title "Compare report",
   :description
   "Write the compare summary report (a PDF listing every change) to path.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "doc.compare"}
  {:name "doc_compare_mark",
   :title "Mark differences as comments",
   :description
   "Add the differences from other (older) to doc (newer) as comments in doc: highlights over replaced (blue) and inserted (green) text, notes where text was deleted (red), authored Compare. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "doc.compare"}
  {:name "form_detect_fields",
   :title "Detect form fields",
   :description
   "Prepare a form ▸ automatic field detection: find the blanks a printed form asks to be filled (underscore runs, lines, empty boxes, rows of comb boxes, small squares for check boxes; on scanned pages read from the pixels) and name each field from its label. With add (default true) the fields are created as one undoable step; otherwise they are only proposed. Returns page (1-based), kind, name and rect (points, origin bottom-left); a row of comb boxes is one text field with comb set to its number of cells, created with the comb flag and that character limit.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.detect"}
  {:name "form_actions",
   :title "Field actions",
   :description
   "Field Properties ▸ Actions: the field's action for each trigger (mouse_up, mouse_down, mouse_enter, mouse_exit, on_focus, on_blur).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.prepare"}
  {:name "form_set_actions",
   :title "Set field actions",
   :description
   "Field Properties ▸ Actions: replace the field's actions. Each item: trigger (mouse_up, mouse_down, mouse_enter, mouse_exit, on_focus, on_blur) and one of javascript (source), url, reset (field names; [] for all), menu (Print, NextPage, PrevPage, FirstPage, LastPage), page (1-based), show / hide (field names), submit (URL). Triggers not listed lose their action. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "form.prepare"}
  {:name "js_enabled",
   :title "JavaScript on or off",
   :description
   "Preferences ▸ JavaScript ▸ Enable Acrobat JavaScript: set it with `enabled`, or read it. With JavaScript off, field scripts other than Acrobat's AF calls don't run.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "ocr_recognize",
   :title "Recognize text (OCR)",
   :description
   "Scan & OCR ▸ Recognize text: render pages, read the words in them and add them as invisible text over the page image, so scanned pages become searchable and selectable (a searchable image; the image is not changed). Pages that already have text are skipped unless skip_text_pages or force_ocr say otherwise; words overlapping existing text are omitted and counted as already_on_page. With output_mode \"editable\" nothing is applied: a NEW document of visible text at the recognised boxes is written to out (which must not be the source; empty pages stay blank). engine and strategy choose the readers (an engine that cannot run is an error named up front); the four preprocessing flags clean the raster first. region reads just that part of one page ([x0, y0, x1, y1] in points from the top-left of the displayed page). Returns each page's recognised text, word count or why it was skipped. Needs the engines (ocr_status). Searchable output is undoable as one step.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.recognize"}
  {:name "ocr_words",
   :title "Words of a recognition (for review)",
   :description
   "The words a recognition finds, for inspection without the GUI: per page, each word's text, its box ([x, y, w, h] in points from the top-left of the displayed page), its confidence and band (high >= 90, medium 70–89, low < 70), which engine read it, and whether it is a suspect (low band). suspects counts the words a reviewer should look at first. Changes nothing on the document. retain_review returns a session-local handle for ocr_review_apply (one per document, at most eight; a new retained recognition replaces the old one). Needs the engines (ocr_status).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "ocr_review_apply",
   :title "Apply or discard reviewed OCR words",
   :description
   "Accept corrected recognition from ocr_words retain_review. Corrections use 1-based page/word positions and text only; empty text removes a word, omitted words keep their original text and boxes. The stored document guard refuses stale, foreign or consumed reviews. Searchable output is one undoable step; editable requires out and writes a new document (out must not exist yet; the review is kept when it does). discard releases the review without applying it. Input is capped at 65536 words and 4 MiB, never truncated.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.correct"}
  {:name "ocr_dictionary",
   :title "Read or update an OCR review dictionary",
   :description
   "Read or add/remove words in an OCR Verify dictionary file (one case-insensitive word per UTF-8 line). Choose its per-language ocr-dictionary-<language>.txt path. Paths honor root; updates are atomic. Refuses invalid words, over 65536 entries or over 4 MiB. No document changes.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.correct"}
  {:name "ocr_recognize_files",
   :title "Recognize text in multiple files",
   :description
   "Scan & OCR ▸ Recognize text ▸ In multiple files: read every page of each PDF in paths and write the searchable result into folder under the same name. skip_text_files leaves whole files that already contain text alone (they are their own skipped bucket, nothing is written); skip_text_pages leaves single text pages alone; force_ocr reads regardless of both. Every output name is checked before the first page is read: two paths sharing a file name (from different folders) are refused, and a file of that name already in folder aborts the batch, with the names in the error. Each written file carries a low_confidence note when words at or under 60 confidence sit on it (1-based sorted pages). Returns, per file, the output path, word count, skipped pages or the error, plus recognized/words/skipped_files totals. Needs the engines (ocr_status).",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.recognize_batch"}
  {:name "ocr_status",
   :title "OCR status",
   :description
   "Whether text recognition is available, where it looks for models (release packages include them; a source build fetches them with `cargo xtask models`; PDFCRAFT_MODELS overrides), its languages, and the engines: ocrs (built in, models) and tesseract (an installed program, with its path).",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "ocr.recognize"}
  {:name "doc_export_all_images",
   :title "Export all images",
   :description
   "Write the images that pages use into a folder (`<name>_Page_<n>_Image_<k>.jpg|png`, n zero-padded to the page count's digits), each once: JPEG images unchanged, others as PNG with their soft mask as alpha. min_size skips images with fewer pixels on their shorter side. Images that can't be decoded yet (JPEG 2000, separations), or past what one export may decode or hold, are listed under skipped, with the reason. Includes unsaved edits.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "export.all_images"}
  {:name "doc_export_text",
   :title "Export text",
   :description
   "Write the reading-order text of pages to a .txt file (pages separated by form feeds).",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "export.text"}
  {:name "fill_sign_date_format",
   :title "Date format for Fill & Sign",
   :description
   "Preferences ▸ Date format: the pattern Fill & Sign dates use (default m/d/yyyy). Set it with `format` (Acrobat date codes yyyy yy mmmm mmm mm m dddd ddd dd d, other runs of y, m or d are refused; H h M s t are time letters and need \\ before them; \\ shows the next character as is), or read it. `language` sets the language of month and weekday names (a code from `languages`, or `auto` to follow the app's interface language; English headless). Returns the format, the language, today in them, `unwritable` (characters of today's date that Fill & Sign can't write into a PDF yet, Western European only; fill_sign_add refuses such a date), the ready-made presets and the languages.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_reduce",
   :title "Reduce file size",
   :description
   "Write a smaller copy of the document to `path` with Acrobat's Reduce File Size choices: colour and grey images above 225 ppi downsampled to 150 ppi and JPEG-compressed (medium quality), black-and-white images averaged down to 300 ppi above 450 ppi and each stored as CCITT Group 4 (or 1-bit Flate, once resampled or packed from more bits) whenever that is smaller, thumbnails dropped, identical fonts and images merged, unused objects dropped, compressed object streams. If the copy wouldn't be smaller, nothing is written and `written` is false. Images past what one run may decode stay as they are, counted in images_refused; streams it only stores with Flate past that stay LZW, uncounted. The open document is unchanged.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "optimize.reduce"}
  {:name "doc_initial_view",
   :title "Initial view",
   :description
   "Read or change how the document opens (Document Properties ▸ Initial View) and its reading options: navigation (page, bookmarks, pages, attachments, layers), layout (default, single, continuous, two_up, two_up_continuous, two_up_cover, two_up_continuous_cover), magnification (default, actual, fit_page, fit_width, fit_height, fit_visible, or a percentage), page, window options (fit_window, center_window, full_screen, display_title), interface options (hide_menubar, hide_toolbar, hide_window_ui), language and binding (left, right). Only the given ones change; returns the result. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_audit_space",
   :title "Audit space usage",
   :description
   "How many bytes each kind of content takes and its share of the file (PDF Optimizer ▸ Audit space usage): images, content streams, fonts, forms, comments, structure, bookmarks, … and document overhead.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "optimize.advanced"}
  {:name "text_lines",
   :title "List text lines",
   :description
   "The lines of existing text on a page (Edit a PDF ▸ Edit text): number, text, box (top-left-origin points), font and size. Use the number with text_edit.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "image_hit",
   :title "Hit test page artwork",
   :description
   "List image/Form numbers whose placement and all clipping paths contain point [x,y] in top-left-origin points. Bezier curves, even-odd/nonzero fill and holes are respected. Read only.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "page_images",
   :title "List page images",
   :description
   "The raster images and grouped Form artwork a page draws (Edit a PDF): number, full placement rect and visible_rect after page/path clipping (top-left-origin points; null if fully hidden), kind (image/form), pixel size ([0,0] for forms) and resource name. Forms include nested graphics and are edited as a whole. Numbers count forms and images together in drawing order, so a page with forms numbers its images differently than before forms were listed: always take numbers from a fresh page_images call.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "image_edit",
   :title "Edit an image",
   :description
   "Change one of a page's images (number from page_images): action move (rect: new full placement box in top-left-origin points, based on page_images.rect), crop (rect: the part to keep, top-left-origin points; the pixels stay in place and page_images.visible_rect shows the result; a later move carries the crop along), remove_crop (remove a crop created by PdfCraft while preserving clipping paths from the original document), rotate (quarters clockwise, default 1), rotate_by (degrees: any angle clockwise about the visible centre; the box in page_images then becomes the turned image's bounding box), transform (matrix: 6 numbers [a, b, c, d, e, f] in top-left-origin points, applied after the current placement so a point (x, y) of the image moves to (a·x + c·y + e, b·x + d·y + f); finite, with a·d − b·c not 0; the box in page_images becomes the transformed image's bounding box), flip_horizontal (reflect left/right on the displayed page), flip_vertical (reflect top/bottom on the displayed page; both flip actions follow the page rotation), replace (path: an image file, drawn in the same place), delete, ungroup (Form artwork only: its content is drawn in place, so its text becomes editable with text_paragraphs/text_edit and its pictures separate; refused for knockout groups and for transparency groups that blend inside, are drawn translucent or blend in a colour space other than the page's, which would composite differently, and for forms whose /DefaultGray, /DefaultRGB or /DefaultCMYK the page doesn't share, which would stop remapping their colours), or arrange: bring_to_front, send_to_back, bring_forward, send_backward (reorder stacking order among content on the page; errors when the image is already at the requested limit; arranging an added image converts it into an ordinary page image). Undoable. The selected image crop transforms with its pixels, isolating shared path scopes while retaining neighboring painting. Text-outline clips return a clear error. Rotation/flip use the visible centre. Form artwork supports move/resize/rotate/flip/delete as a group; replace and image_save only support raster images.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "image_save",
   :title "Save image as",
   :description
   "Write one of a page's raster images (number from page_images; forms are refused) to path: JPEG images unchanged, others as PNG (the extension is added when missing).",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive true,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_font_files",
   :title "List installed document fonts",
   :description
   "Discover openly licensed, embeddable TrueType/OpenType files on request. Optional directories (at most 16) restrict the scan; with --root, only that root is scanned by default and supplied folders must stay inside it. The scan skips symlinks, collections and invalid/licence-restricted fonts, with depth, entry and byte budgets. Select a returned path with text_font_import.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_font_import",
   :title "Load document font",
   :description
   "Load an explicitly selected, openly licensed full TrueType/OpenType face into a page. The program's family, embedding permissions and licence declaration are validated. Completes source subsets of the same face without replacing existing glyphs. Returns a font resource usable with text_edit.font_resource. Undoable; respects root confinement. No system-interface fallback is exported.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_fonts",
   :title "List document fonts",
   :description
   "List validated embedded source faces and approved full preview faces for a page. Full registered resources and bundled choices can be selected by text_edit.font_resource. builtin:thai explicitly replaces a paragraph or range with the bundled Noto Sans Thai; a build without that face never lists it and text_edit refuses it there (a page whose fonts fill the listing budget may also omit it, but text_edit still accepts it). preview_only faces cannot be selected.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_prepare",
   :title "Prepare grouped text",
   :description
   "Make existing text inside supported Form XObjects directly editable on one page. Replaces placements with their original operators and resources, preserving position, clipping and other pages. Refuses unsafe transparency, tags or malformed content. Adds no text or cover boxes. Returns prepared_groups (placements made editable), repaired_fonts (damaged legacy Thai maps repaired) and refused_groups ('name: reason' for each group left as it was). Also repairs the page's own damaged legacy Thai maps, grouped or not. Fails when the page has nothing to prepare or repair. Undoable; list text_paragraphs again afterwards.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_paragraphs",
   :title "List paragraphs",
   :description
   "The paragraphs on a page (adjacent source runs grouped into aligned visual rows, including mixed fonts, sizes and colours): number, text, editor_text (visual rows separated by newlines), rows and source line numbers, box (top-left-origin points), font and size. Use the number with text_edit's paragraph: until you list the page again, a number names the paragraph listed here, even after edits regroup the page.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_edit_layout",
   :title "Measure text draft",
   :description
   "Measure a paragraph draft using the same PDF rewrite as Apply, without changing the document. Returns source_rect, draft_rect (top-left-origin points), overflow, and the embedded sfnt source faces available to the inline editor. Text defaults to the unchanged paragraph. Optional size, width, font_resource and disjoint UTF-8 ranges preview formatting changes.",
   :read-only true,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_edit",
   :title "Edit text",
   :description
   "Replace the text of one paragraph (paragraph, from text_paragraphs: rewrapped to the paragraph's width with its line spacing) or one line (line, from text_lines) in place, keeping position, size and colour. For a mixed-style region, editor_text supplies visual row breaks; surviving text keeps its source-run styles and inserted text inherits the surrounding run. For a paragraph, also change its formatting: font (helvetica, times, courier) with bold/italic, size (points), color (#rrggbb), align (left, center, right, justify), underline, line_spacing (× size), char_spacing (points) and scale (horizontal, percent), or move it (dx, dy in points; up is +dy) and rewrap it to a new width (points); text may then be omitted. Its own font is reused when it can show every character and no font/weight change is requested; otherwise it uses a standard font matching the source style or, for text no standard font can show, real fallback outlines from PdfCraft's own faces, from the one that has every character: the craft-fonts Japanese faces (Mincho/Gothic matching the requested/source family and available weight) or, behind them, the bundled Inter face, which carries the Latin, Greek and Cyrillic letters they lack (Uzbek қ, Kazakh ә). The result shows the font used, and for a paragraph its text unless the document's security doesn't allow copying. Missing Japanese weights use Regular, not synthetic bold; the small web build has only Gothic Regular. Paragraph bold may be set without font to keep the source family. Text that no available font can show is refused. A paragraph number is refused when an earlier edit merged that paragraph into a neighbour (list the page again); the result's stale_paragraphs names the numbers gone. Undoable.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "text_script",
   :title "Superscript or subscript",
   :description
   "Format text ▸ Superscript or Subscript on one paragraph (paragraph, from text_paragraphs), or on range [start, end): UTF-8 byte offsets of its editor_text. The characters take the Unicode superscript or subscript forms (2 → ², 2 → ₂; the font must have those glyphs, and extracted text contains them); text already in that script goes back to plain characters. Characters Unicode has no such form for (q, a space) stay unchanged and do not determine the selection's script state. Mixed plain and target-script characters normalize to that script, then to plain text on the next call (H₂2 → H₂₂ → H22); a second toggle does not reconstruct the original mixture. Use Undo to restore the exact prior text. The paragraph is then rewritten as text_edit rewrites it, with the same result fields. Refused when no character would change. Undoable. Mathematical minus U+2212 has its own script mapping; ASCII hyphen-minus stays unchanged.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "edit.edit_text"}
  {:name "doc_revisions",
   :title "List revisions",
   :description
   "List the document's saved revisions (oldest first): each incremental update is one. Returns revision number, where it ends in the file and its size, and which signatures sign exactly that revision.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_open_revision",
   :title "Open a revision",
   :description
   "Open saved revision `revision` (1 = the oldest) of a document as a new, unsaved document, to see the file as it was then.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs"}
  {:name "doc_optimize",
   :title "Optimize PDF",
   :description
   "Write an optimized copy to `path` (Acrobat's PDF Optimizer). preset: standard (default; Reduce File Size's choices) or mobile (images to 96 ppi above 144, JPEG high quality); the options below change it. compatibility: retain (default; keeps the document's version, or 1.5 when object streams are written), 1.4, 1.5, 1.6, 1.7 or 2.0. merge_fragments (default true) first puts a page picture drawn as many stacked image strips (as some PDF printers write it) back together into one image, so it can be resampled (merged_images, fragments_merged). color / gray: { downsample, ppi, above_ppi, compression: jpeg|zip|retain, quality 1–100 } (defaults: downsample to 150 ppi above 225, JPEG 60). mono: { downsample, ppi, above_ppi, compression: ccitt_g4|jbig2|retain } for black-and-white images and image masks (default: averaged down to 300 ppi above 450 ppi, counted in images_resampled; stored losslessly as CCITT Group 4 or JBIG2 (or 1-bit Flate, once resampled or packed from more bits) when that is smaller, up to 16 JBIG2 images sharing one symbol dictionary (/JBIG2Globals) where that is smaller still (image masks and DeviceGray images named directly, of at most 64 Mi pixels, which redaction can store again without it), Group 3 fax images, JBIG2 images, black-and-white RGB and indexed images using only palette entries 0 and 1 among them, counted in images_recompressed; a picture's stencil /Mask and one-bit /SMask are stored again the same way, at their size, not resampled and sharing no dictionary, counted as images; retain resamples only, a CCITT image staying CCITT, a JBIG2 image JBIG2 and any other becoming Flate). Images past what one run may decode stay as they are, counted in images_refused; streams it only stores with Flate past that stay LZW, uncounted. Images are measured where pages draw them and replaced only when smaller. discard_*: thumbnails (default true), alternate_images (true), tags, search_index (removes the catalog's /PieceInfo entries whose application name contains \"index\" in any letter case; search_indexes), print_settings (entries removed: print_settings), form_actions (submit, import and reset actions removed: form_actions; the fields and links stay, and the actions chained after one still run); flate_unencoded (true); object_streams (default true; always off for 1.4); lzw_to_flate (true) decodes LZW streams and stores them with Flate instead, leaving any it cannot decode unchanged (lzw_streams counts the streams converted); remove_invalid_links and remove_unreferenced_dests (true); discard_external_refs takes GoToR, GoToE, Launch and ImportData actions, and Thread actions with /F, out of links and bookmarks, removes a link left with nothing to do, and keeps links within the document and web links (external_links, external_bookmarks); images and forms the pages list but never draw are always dropped (unused_xobjects). discard: Remove Hidden Information categories (metadata, attachments, comments, form-fields, hidden-text, hidden-layers, bookmarks, links-actions-scripts, private-data). Signed documents are refused. target_bytes (optional): if the copy is larger, retry with up to 5 progressively stronger image settings (downsample to at most 110, 96, 72, 54, 36 ppi, applied to colour and grey images; images set to JPEG also get JPEG quality at most 45, 35, 28, 20, 12, while zip and retain images keep their encoding and only get the lower ppi) and stop at the first copy that fits; reports target_reached, attempts and target_settings, and writes the smallest copy with target_reached false when none fits. Without it nothing changes. The open document is unchanged.",
   :read-only false,
   :destructive false,
   :source "crates/automation/src/tools.rs",
   :command "optimize.advanced"}
  {:name "doc_flatten",
